      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That fear of nowhere to stand is the fear of true freedom, which is terrifying because it demands you face the void directly. If letting go feels like a final destination, perhaps you can view it as a gentle deceleration, not a catastrophic fall. You don't have to leap off; you can just ease the pedal, allowing the treadmill to slow down to a barely perceptible hum.",
      "source": "target",
